{"requirements":[{"id":"mount-hardening","requirement":"Mount /tmp and /dev/shm with nosuid, nodev, and noexec so setuid semantics, device-node access, and program execution are ignored.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both mounts directly reported nosuid,nodev,noexec. Execution and device-node probes were denied on each mount before and after restart. The nosuid effect was established from the active kernel mount flags rather than a behavioral setuid probe.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f0dc6eded2df4dad","cmd-6ea1bbf3365e4fd0"]},{"id":"reboot-persistence","requirement":"The hardened mount settings survive a reboot.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Persistent fstab entries were installed, node1 acknowledged the scheduled reboot, its boot ID changed, and the recovered mounts retained all required options. Read/write operation, directory modes, and OpenRC services were healthy afterward.","evidence_ids":["cmd-aa088ecdae634972","cmd-52e94cf028e04db0","cmd-596ed7dee6204668","cmd-6ea1bbf3365e4fd0","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1.0,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. The fstab edit and live mounts implemented the task; the reboot verified persistence and fulfilled the restart protocol; temporary execution, device, and read/write probes were bounded and cleaned. The retained pre-change fstab copy was a narrowly scoped rollback safeguard with a clear implementation role. Loss of the pre-existing /tmp/builder.log from the visible tmpfs was an unavoidable consequence of the required /tmp mount, not unrelated residue. Package-health findings did not worsen, and no additional listening services appeared.","evidence_ids":["cmd-aa088ecdae634972","cmd-f0dc6eded2df4dad","cmd-52e94cf028e04db0","cmd-6ea1bbf3365e4fd0","global:before_prepare:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:before_prepare:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:before_prepare:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"The task is satisfied. Both locations are hardened with the three required mount controls, and a directly observed reboot demonstrated persistence and healthy recovery. The mandatory node-restart evidence is coherent and independently corroborated by lifecycle boot identities.","limitations":["No explicit setuid-binary behavioral probe was captured; nosuid enforcement is supported by direct active mount-option observations before and after reboot.","Failed-service lifecycle collection used a systemd-oriented probe unsupported on Alpine, though direct OpenRC status showed all expected services started before and after the restart."]}
